            <div xml:id="d627">

                <pb facs="0528" n="516" xml:id="pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00114A European War 1939/103: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-10T23:00:00+01:00">November 10,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 10—9:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>585. My 584, November 10, 10 p.m. General Rios Capape, Commander of the military
                    district of Tetuán personally accompanied me in visiting the American internees
                    and introduced me to the officers of his garrison who were looking after the
                    welfare of the men. He and his officers could not have been more cordial in
                    their assurances to accord our men every possible amenity.</p>
                <p>I asked General Capape whether it would be agreeable if Colonel Johnson, our
                    Military Attaché, or one of his assistants might visit the men and he
                    immediately replied that any member of the Legation would be given every
                    possible facility to visit these men and to provide for their welfare at any
                    time. Booth is proceeding to Targuist tomorrow to look after the welfare of the
                    American internees there.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
